to a hopeful agnostic,

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.750
is what I called it at the time.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.593
I don't really refer to that label a lot,

00:03:54.371 --> 00:03:57.040
but that's, I still think that applies.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.480
And that story, cover my entire life.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.480
You know, there were snapshots
from age 10 and on, right.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.850
But today I'm only covering the last year.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:12.783
So it's a different thing.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.945
I mean, it's been a crazy year,

00:04:15.945 --> 00:04:19.610
and it's been a tough one
for everybody on this planet.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.320
Of course, to varying degrees,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.510
but it's been a crazy year.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:27.760
And over this past year, I was blindsided

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.760
by a number of difficult
challenges that I would have,

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.793
as an evangelical Christian,
have labeled as test of faith.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.870
Meaning something happens in your life,

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:45.470
and your response to it reveals

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.013
what you truly and deeply believe.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.170
I didn't think of the things
that I'm gonna share today

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:55.320
in that way as they were happening.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:58.280
And I think that's kind of
part of what I wanna share

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.540
and how I did process those things.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:04.240
But, you know, in kind of
a compare and contrast,

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.170
I realized that's how my former self

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.480
would see the things I went through

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:09.633
as test of faith.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.860
To put it even more
specifically, in the past,

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.840
as a Christian, I shuddered at the thought

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.840
of facing suffering, facing
fear, and facing loss

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.810
without the peace that accompanied

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.163
a very specific believe about Jesus.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.920
- I think that something that
a lot of people can relate to.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.640
I know for me, when you
think about the potential

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.600
of not having God in your
life in the same way,

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.120
or not having that
relationship with Jesus,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.713
in the way that you said
you did in the past,

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:50.320
you're like, even in transition,

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.110
I know you talked to me a lot about this.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.770
As we were sort of transitioning,

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:59.030
there was this fear of is
something horrible gonna happen,

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.980
and I won't be able to make it through,

00:06:01.903 --> 00:06:05.110
because I've always had this idea

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.360
that you'd retreat

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.701
into sort of, you have
refuge in the Lord, you know,

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:11.650
as you're going through those things.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.920
- And that is what we,
that was our practice.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.037
And that was our experience.

00:06:15.037 --> 00:06:17.990
And that is where we
found a source of strength

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.103
in our relationships with Christ.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:27.590
So, you know, having that be
a defining aspect of any test

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:33.480
I faced in my life, yeah, it was,

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:38.240
I shuddered at the thought
of that that being gone.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:42.880
Yet here I was, over this past year

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.640
facing suffering, facing
fear, facing loss,

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.150
after having moved on from that faith.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:50.590
- And that's what really
keeps a lot of people

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:55.590
from walking away, frankly.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.780
- So I just wanna share three experiences

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.133
from this past year.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:03.750
But before I do that,

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.310
I just wanna go ahead and say that,

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:10.453
I'm in a really good place
right now, spiritually.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:16.540
I don't look back on, on my
former life as an evangelical,

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.060
and wish that I was still there.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:22.080
You know, if you think, if you go back

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.320
and listen to my story,
there's lots of things

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.820
that you know, that I
appreciate and that I value

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.723
from that experience.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.410
It's by no means all negative.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:38.686
And I've, you know I
already talked about that.

00:07:38.686 --> 00:07:42.710
But I, you know as I go
through these things,

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:43.550
I just don't, you know,

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.040
I just kinda wanna head off at the pass

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:47.180
that like, "Oh, I feel sorry for you."

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:50.530
And, you know, I don't wanna elicit pity,

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.910
because that's not my point at all.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.707
I'm gonna be very honest about
how I process these things

00:07:56.707 --> 00:07:58.760
and the emotional
component and all of that.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:03.760
But I think it's the fact that you know,

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:09.050
I found a way forward that
alleviated those fears

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.830
that my former self had.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.270
So yeah, I don't look
back and wish I was there.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:19.270
I'm happy, but I am also restless.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.400
I don't know if that's
exactly the right word,

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.573
because I mean it in only a good way.

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:28.710
But I'm restless in the sense

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.990
that I'd like to think that my spirit,

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.400
or whatever you wanna
call it within myself,

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:38.640
is staying open to where I'm headed.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.363
Even though that ultimate
destination is unknown to me.

00:08:44.866 --> 00:08:46.540
(chuckles)

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.760
But I'm doing my best,
to be honest with myself,

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.520
and honest with those that love me,

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.670
and honest right now with you listening.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:09:00.670
And I feel hopeful, and I'm
at peace with my direction.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:07.450
And today is another day
on that journey for me.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:10.010
And a big component of that,

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:14.410
is it being an active,
spiritual journey, that I'm on.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:18.500
And I'm grateful to be doing
this particular podcast

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:22.393
to kind of put another
stake in the ground to say,

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:25.890
a year later, this is
how I'm processing it.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:30.360
And this is where I'm at but it's, I mean,

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:34.030
I'm sure this will get
heavy, but it's overall,

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.540
I just wanted to, you
know, I wanna bookend it

00:09:37.526 --> 00:09:42.526
with this message that is
a positive message for me,

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:45.080
that I'm in a good place.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.650
- And I'm glad you're saying that,

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.973
because, you know I think that,

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.060
as you contrast the way that we approach

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:54.210
these kinds of things, right,

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.563
and the way that we approached
our original stories,

00:09:55.563 --> 00:09:57.880
and the way I'm sure we're gonna approach

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.180
the sort of the follow-up,

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:03.470
is you kind of explore things

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:06.573
through your personal
experience and story.

00:10:07.906 --> 00:10:10.786
And you're also a verbal processor.

00:10:10.786 --> 00:10:15.786
You also, you know, you aren't
quite as sure of yourself,

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:17.783
and that's, I mean,

00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:21.680
I think that is a positive
thing for you, ultimately.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.940
I can be a little too confident,

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.540
and a little too sure in
the things that I'm saying,

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:29.300
and a lot of times it'll
just piss people off.

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:34.260
But sometimes when you're being
very vulnerable and honest

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:38.280
about where you're at, and
the fact that you know,

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:41.690
you're just being honest
in your uncertainty.

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:43.907
I think a lot of people are sort of like,

00:10:43.907 --> 00:10:45.900
"Oh, poor Link."

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.380
And that's not at all what
you've meant to communicate.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.530
And so I'm glad you're
saying that up front,

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:55.490
because I know you, and I know
where you're at spiritually,

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:57.630
and I know that it's not
a place to be pitied.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:58.463
- Absolutely not.

00:10:58.463 --> 00:10:59.900
That's exactly what I'm trying to get at.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:01.780
And I think that when you mention,

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:06.780
you know my style you know,
it's not as assertive,

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.160
and maybe when it comes to certain things

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:13.210
I don't assert confidence in
certain things that I believe,

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.720
especially when, what I'm asserting

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.530
is embracing uncertainty.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.920
But I also think that
a little bit of that,

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.330
well I don't know how much of it,

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:28.330
but a factor that kinda drives that in me

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:32.003
is kind of reacting to,

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.670
I just have a negative reaction

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.320
to when people assert something

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.230
that I just don't believe you
can know with 100% certainty,

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:41.063
it bothers me.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:45.180
So it's not my instinct to do that.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.253
You know, I share my experience,

00:11:48.907 --> 00:11:51.750
draw your own conclusions.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:54.100
Or just, you know another
thing I'm learning

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:57.270
is that you can truly listen to somebody,

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.040
you can truly empathize with somebody.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.830
And it's not always
about making a decision

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:03.520
or a judgment about them.

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:06.530
That's something that I realized

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.350
that I thought, for some reason

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:10.680
I thought I had to operate that way.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:12.980
- Well, that's the
world that we come from.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:16.450
When you're in a system,
when you encounter things,

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.840
you have to file them into your system.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:22.070
And so we've kind of been
trained for a lifetime,

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:25.440
of systematizing people into an ideology,

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:28.190
and we're trying really hard
to not continue to so that.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:32.060
- There's a way to be
impacted by empathetically,

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.483
interacting with somebody that's not,

00:12:35.547 --> 00:12:38.010
that judgment doesn't have
to be a component of it.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:42.623
And you know, which brings
me to the fact that like,

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:47.960
a year later, yeah, I
don't have any more answers

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:51.400
than I had a year ago. (chuckles)

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:55.660
But I'll tell you, I
do believe that my soul

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:59.800
is richer because I've made some progress,

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.883
in knowing, and loving myself more.

00:13:02.953 --> 00:13:05.280
And that's through therapy,
through introspection,

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:06.733
through conversations.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:11.730
And I'm beginning to experience,

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:15.420
how understanding and accepting myself

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.833
has expanded my capacity
to love other people.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.220
That's where I felt like I've needed

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:26.543
to focus a lot of my
energy for the past year,

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:29.733
in terms of my spiritual journey.

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:35.600
And, you know, I feel like,

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.150
for Christy and I, as a couple,

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:40.713
just to kind of talk about the
two of us for a little bit.

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:47.863
This journey is really stretching us.

00:13:48.761 --> 00:13:49.990
And I mean, really good stretching

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.830
is really not comfortable. (chuckles)

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:55.210
You know, sometimes it hurts a little,

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:57.903
it needs to hurt in the right way,

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:03.880
so that ultimately it's strengthening,

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:07.404
and definitely the experiences

00:14:07.404 --> 00:14:09.683
that we're going through together,

00:14:10.705 --> 00:14:12.790
and the spiritual
components of that included

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.003
are strengthening our bond.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:22.160
So, we're good on that
front too. (chuckles)

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.140
Christy really helped me figure out

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.203
what I wanted to say today.

00:14:27.084 --> 00:14:30.270
And, you know, as I was
kind of prepping it,

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.343
you know, I texted her yesterday,

00:14:34.694 --> 00:14:35.527
and I sent something to her,

00:14:35.527 --> 00:14:37.913
and I just also told
her how much I love us.

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:42.170
And she replied and said, "I love us too.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:45.060
I want you to feel freedom
and embrace this journey

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:46.860
that you are on."

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.980
Heart emoji.

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:52.570
And it meant so much you
know, to have her support,

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:57.570
and to say, "Be free, embrace
what you're going through."

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:02.960
You know, it's not, you're
not a victim of something.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.990
You know this is a journey to be embraced,

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:08.400
to be celebrated and you know,

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:13.400
but I'm just so grateful that she can,

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:16.493
she loves me in that
way, and that she can,

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.253
she can send me that text, you know.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.570
I don't think I'd be able
to share these things

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:24.430
publicly right now, without her support.

00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:25.453
I know I wouldn't.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:33.110
And people also wonder about
our kids in this process.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.740
So, you know, I wanna talk about that

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.193
just a little bit too.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:44.950
Honestly, I mean, there are times

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:49.130
when the fear creeps back in

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.810
that maybe we've done them a disservice,

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.693
by not raising them in the church.

00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:58.883
But I don't believe that,

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:04.323
because I see them, I know their hearts.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:09.490
I mean, while there may be
things they missed out on,

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:12.573
there are many pitfalls, they were spared.

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:17.870
And you know, I look at
Lily, I look at Lincoln,

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:21.790
I look at Lando, and I know them.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:26.790
You know, they're
wholehearted, wonderful humans.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:30.683
And I admire them so
much for who they are.

00:16:31.877 --> 00:16:35.550
And I'm proud of them.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:39.063
And I don't regret the,

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:45.963
I don't regret the
trajectory of our lives,

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.040
and you know, how we parented them.

00:16:54.742 --> 00:16:56.180
And I stand by it overall.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:57.920
You know, I'm very flawed.

00:16:57.920 --> 00:16:59.940
And, but I think it's important

00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:02.220
that they could articulate those flaws.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:03.533
- Well, I know, I think,

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:09.690
one of the things that
both of us have encountered

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:11.923
post-deconstruction as a dad,

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:17.970
is within the church, within
the evangelical church,

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:22.520
there is an expectation
that the dad, the father,

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.920
is the spiritual leader of the household.

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:25.753
- Yeah.

00:17:25.753 --> 00:17:28.680
Based on a lot of things,
mostly just patriarchy.

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:32.610
But, and there's an expectation

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:34.390
that not only would the dad be a leader,

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:35.870
but the dad has the answers.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.010
- Right.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.210
- Right, and the dad sets
the tone, sets the pace,

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:41.370
he leads his family.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.070
And I mean-

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:46.240
- And he's held accountable to that.

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:49.929
- Well, but also as a Christian man,

00:17:49.929 --> 00:17:53.820
as Christian dad, there's this expectation

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:54.880
that you'll have the answers,

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.410
and that there's very few things

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:57.950
that you won't have answers to.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:59.940
And there is a playbook for everything

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:03.240
that your kids, or your
wife might encounter.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:04.923
First of all, a lot of pressure.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:07.730
But I think in my case,

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:11.030
there was a lot of sort of
just playing along with that,

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:13.330
being like I don't really
have the answers to this,

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:15.090
but I can point you to an answer

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:17.390
that we sort of collectively
as a community come up with.

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:19.840
And I think one of the
biggest things as a father,

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:23.069
is when there is true uncertainty,

00:18:23.069 --> 00:18:26.800
there are situations that
do not have an answer,

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.630
and being able to say, "I don't know."

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.719
I don't know if there's
a satisfactory answer

00:18:33.719 --> 00:18:35.049
to this question that you have.

00:18:35.049 --> 00:18:37.200
I don't know if there's
a satisfactory solution

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:41.720
to this situation, but we
can figure it out together.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.980
And that's, if you've had something,

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:47.670
if you had a system, and you
no longer have the system,

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:50.330
you can feel that fear
that you're talking about.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:52.700
It's like, man, they're
going through this right now.

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:54.800
And if I just, I'm not
sure it's the right answer,

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.960
but it is an answer
that I could be getting

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:59.830
from my former belief system.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:03.120
And now I'm just saying, "I don't know."

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.700
And you feel a little bit,

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.753
you feel like a failure a little bit.

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:12.940
- Yeah, I mean, Lilly's turning 18,

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.970
she's leaving the house,
go off to college,

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:19.413
and you know being adult.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:23.510
But, and you know everything
I said a few seconds ago

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:26.510
still stands, but I have
noticed that there's times

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:31.190
when I would not, I think I
would opt to not say something

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.383
because it would be,

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.900
the instinct is in the lack of an answer,

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.220
it's hard to make something

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:43.383
a teachable moment when
what you're conveying

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:49.040
is embracing uncertainty
and the truth of that.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.910
And it's, you know, I think
some things will come clear

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:55.649
as I continue talking about-

00:19:55.649 --> 00:19:56.482
- It would come true too. (laughing)

00:19:56.482 --> 00:19:58.020
- Come true. (laughing)

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:01.263
As I, you know, will come clear about,

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.640
what I continue to
wrestle with from my past,

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:10.027
and how it impacts my
point of view on myself

00:20:10.027 --> 00:20:13.710
and my relationships with
Christy and the kids,

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.210
and other people.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:20.210
But, you know, I'm trying
to take a more active effort

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:24.590
to have conversations,
open-ended conversations

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.970
where these topics are not taboo,

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.380
just because you don't have an answer

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:29.860
doesn't make it taboo.

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:32.020
It doesn't make you
something to be ashamed of.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:35.130
You know, it's like, this is real,

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:40.050
and let's not be afraid
to talk about it openly,

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:40.943
as a family.

00:20:43.017 --> 00:20:47.487
So I mean, just to complete that point,

00:20:47.487 --> 00:20:50.440
when I look at my
relationship with myself,

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:52.719
my relationship with
Christy and with our kids,

00:20:52.719 --> 00:20:55.970
I am so grateful for what we have,

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:59.760
and I'm relieved, (chuckles) honestly.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:03.210
Because like we said, there was a time,

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:05.683
for most of my life, in fact,

00:21:07.050 --> 00:21:09.480
when I firmly believed
that those relationships

00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:14.480
could not flourish and weather
life storms apart from Jesus.

00:21:17.021 --> 00:21:22.021
So, you know, with all
that we shared last year,

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:28.700
and I still struggle with
giving myself permission

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:35.720
to outright say this,
but if there is no God,

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:36.670
I'm okay with that.

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:42.653
In fact, I'm even good with that.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.690
I'm not sayin' I prefer that,

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:48.110
but I'm sayin' I'm even good with it.

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:52.143
I have accepted that
as a real possibility,

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:55.350
and I think I'm at peace with it.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.560
Maybe there's a loving God,

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:00.740
and I'm open and hopeful that there is,

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:04.283
but I'm also good if I never find out.

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:09.533
Because there's just no
guarantee that I will find out.

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:14.790
In the meantime part of
my spiritual practice

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:18.440
is processing and shedding,

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:20.350
the guilt and baggage of judgment

00:22:20.350 --> 00:22:22.650
that I've carried for
the majority of my life.

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:27.640
Maybe my point of view on
these things that I've stated,

00:22:28.832 --> 00:22:31.100
you know maybe they sound
like harsh statements.

00:22:31.100 --> 00:22:34.590
I think about people who love me

00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:36.617
who would hear me say
those things and I'm like,

00:22:36.617 --> 00:22:39.190
"Well, maybe I could have
taken the edge off of that."

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:43.113
And maybe my perspective
will change over time,

00:22:44.808 --> 00:22:45.641
but that's where I'm at,

00:22:45.641 --> 00:22:48.830
I don't wanna be embarrassed
or ashamed of it.

00:22:48.830 --> 00:22:50.690
Or like I said,

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:52.910
I wanna shed the guilt
and baggage of judgment

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:56.670
that comes along with
me saying that out loud

00:22:56.670 --> 00:22:59.283
to who knows how many people.

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:03.730
I mean that's just a big part
of my personal work right now,

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:07.380
because I mean, at 42,

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:10.020
I hopefully have even more life to live,

00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:11.770
then I've already lived.

00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:13.010
- Ah, so at least 84.

00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:15.660
- Yeah, I'm aimin' for 85. (chuckles)

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:17.423
- Well, that was, I mean, I don't know,

00:23:17.423 --> 00:23:21.920
that would be currently beyond
the average life expectancy

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:23.150
of an American male.

00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:24.100
- Keep that to yourself.

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:26.870
- But I have to believe that that'll keep,

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:29.540
I think it's actually
has reversed recently.

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:31.890
And livin' in California and
breathing in all this smog,

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:33.450
you're probably not doing yourself,

00:23:33.450 --> 00:23:36.033
I'm just sayin', ah you'll
be lucky to get to 84.

00:23:37.550 --> 00:23:38.900
- Well, okay.

00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:42.670
Given that it seems that
half of my life is over,

00:23:42.670 --> 00:23:45.040
I'm gonna live the life that I have,

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:47.680
and I'm wanna embrace it wholeheartedly.

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:48.930
You know, I wanna move forward

00:23:48.930 --> 00:23:52.870
embracing the now that I have been gifted.

00:23:52.870 --> 00:23:53.703
- Yeah.

00:23:54.560 --> 00:23:56.170
- And I can say that I've been gifted,

00:23:56.170 --> 00:23:59.230
even though I don't know
even if there's a giver,

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:01.893
but I hope there is. (chuckles)

00:24:03.840 --> 00:24:08.840
So I'm ready to share
some of my experiences,

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:13.020
three of them over the past year

00:24:13.020 --> 00:24:16.610
that have helped define what
my spiritual journey looks like

00:24:16.610 --> 00:24:17.833
up to this point.

00:24:22.290 --> 00:24:25.830
Like I said, you know, for me to say

00:24:25.830 --> 00:24:26.830
it's been a difficult year.

00:24:26.830 --> 00:24:29.848
You know, I can keep acknowledging

00:24:29.848 --> 00:24:31.780
how people have it more difficult,

00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:34.040
or how it's been a difficult
year for so many people,

00:24:34.040 --> 00:24:38.983
but you know, just, it has
been a long and difficult year.

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:45.400
And there was a pretty lengthy buildup

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:48.960
to my nanny passing away.

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:49.810
You know, I mentioned that

00:24:49.810 --> 00:24:54.810
as one of my most meaningful
moments of last year.

00:24:57.350 --> 00:24:59.190
Of course that's my mom's mom.

00:24:59.190 --> 00:25:03.483
And she had a sense that
her life was winding down.

00:25:04.490 --> 00:25:07.223
So I was the one to help
her get her will in order.

00:25:08.391 --> 00:25:10.360
And it wasn't just one conversation,

00:25:10.360 --> 00:25:11.850
you know it's like the whole process,

00:25:11.850 --> 00:25:14.977
including getting her
to a lawyer and talking.

00:25:14.977 --> 00:25:17.810
Everything that went along with it,

00:25:17.810 --> 00:25:20.480
it's just a number of months, you know.

00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:22.963
And it's all happening over the phone.

00:25:24.396 --> 00:25:28.080
And, (deep sighing) you know,
she loved me her whole life.

00:25:32.220 --> 00:25:35.943
And in the end I just couldn't
be there, to just hug her.

00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:42.440
And, you know, it's so
much of our communication

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:46.610
was just about me helping her find peace

00:25:46.610 --> 00:25:49.540
with this outlying thing
associated with her will,

00:25:49.540 --> 00:25:52.650
which I, you know I was very glad to do.

00:25:52.650 --> 00:25:57.253
But it's, you know,
it's I felt frustrated,

00:25:58.698 --> 00:26:02.650
and I felt helpless, and I felt sad.

00:26:02.650 --> 00:26:06.850
You know, it's just, you find yourself,

00:26:06.850 --> 00:26:09.060
it's different when you're
just having a phone call

00:26:09.060 --> 00:26:10.733
and you find yourself having,

00:26:11.597 --> 00:26:14.860
"Oh, this is the last phone call."

00:26:14.860 --> 00:26:19.300
You know, I'm saying something to her

00:26:19.300 --> 00:26:21.453
that is different
because you're not there.

00:26:23.480 --> 00:26:27.920
And then you're not there
for the family afterward.

00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:32.683
I mean, it was tough you know.

00:26:33.940 --> 00:26:38.940
And you know of course I wanted to hope

00:26:39.890 --> 00:26:41.773
that she was in heaven.

00:26:45.840 --> 00:26:48.113
All of me believes there is no hell,

00:26:49.690 --> 00:26:51.970
but a big part of me believes

00:26:51.970 --> 00:26:53.950
that there might not be a heaven either.

00:26:53.950 --> 00:26:55.823
We just cease to exist.

00:26:57.520 --> 00:27:02.520
But I mean that's, you know okay.

00:27:02.650 --> 00:27:04.590
That's what I, hold that thought,

00:27:04.590 --> 00:27:06.140
I hold that belief in my mind,

00:27:06.140 --> 00:27:07.900
but it gets difficult to wrestle with

00:27:07.900 --> 00:27:10.943
when you've got one more loved
one on the other side, right.

00:27:15.230 --> 00:27:20.230
But, it didn't change the
conclusions I've already come to.

00:27:22.290 --> 00:27:27.290
You know, I think of a fear of death,

00:27:30.020 --> 00:27:33.170
and a desire for eternal life

00:27:33.170 --> 00:27:38.170
for my loved ones, and
myself is very appealing,

00:27:38.330 --> 00:27:42.620
but it's not, you know
that's not the foundation

00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:43.970
for what I believe.

00:27:43.970 --> 00:27:48.970
It's like a benefit, I felt like.

00:27:52.970 --> 00:27:54.880
So, it's I don't know-

00:27:54.880 --> 00:27:56.160
- Although it might be the foundation

00:27:56.160 --> 00:27:57.900
for religion in general.

00:27:57.900 --> 00:27:58.733
- Hm.

00:27:58.733 --> 00:27:59.769
- Just.

00:27:59.769 --> 00:28:02.670
- It just didn't change my conclusions.

00:28:02.670 --> 00:28:06.110
I didn't find myself as I was hurting,

00:28:06.110 --> 00:28:07.470
and I was wrestling with that,

00:28:07.470 --> 00:28:11.810
or I was, you know I
was writing her eulogy,

00:28:11.810 --> 00:28:13.470
to give to somebody else to read.

00:28:13.470 --> 00:28:18.083
You know, it was all of those feelings.

00:28:21.060 --> 00:28:26.060
It didn't lead to doubt, honestly.

00:28:26.710 --> 00:28:30.210
It was just you know, of
course she's gonna die.

00:28:30.210 --> 00:28:32.120
Of course, we're all gonna die.

00:28:32.120 --> 00:28:36.880
It's just, you know, it was kind of this,

00:28:36.880 --> 00:28:39.340
I have these conclusions,
and I have this pain,

00:28:39.340 --> 00:28:44.340
and I'm aware that these
things will happen. (chuckles)

00:28:45.260 --> 00:28:46.200
So...

00:28:51.240 --> 00:28:55.320
I'm left with I don't know, you know.

00:28:55.320 --> 00:28:58.300
Do I know, can I assert where she is?

00:28:58.300 --> 00:29:00.340
Can I give that comfort?

00:29:00.340 --> 00:29:03.103
Can I comfort myself or
my loved ones in that way?

00:29:03.977 --> 00:29:06.193
I don't know, who really does?

00:29:08.060 --> 00:29:11.450
So I celebrated her
life as much as I could.

00:29:11.450 --> 00:29:14.520
And I talked to my family and processed it

00:29:14.520 --> 00:29:16.080
as much as I could.

00:29:16.080 --> 00:29:17.760
And I tried to embrace the grief

00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:22.760
to make it as real as
possible without being there.

00:29:22.889 --> 00:29:26.190
And accept something we all know,

00:29:26.190 --> 00:29:28.130
that death is a part of life.

00:29:28.130 --> 00:29:33.130
And that this is a part
of my spiritual exercise.

00:29:39.660 --> 00:29:41.093
I couldn't have predicted,

00:29:42.210 --> 00:29:44.550
beforehand that that's how
I would have interacted

00:29:44.550 --> 00:29:45.463
with all of it.

00:29:47.890 --> 00:29:49.030
And, you know, there'll be another way

00:29:49.030 --> 00:29:51.470
when I eventually do get to go home,

00:29:51.470 --> 00:29:54.720
and, you know help get
everything in order,

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:57.370
that's still around at
the house and stuff,

00:29:57.370 --> 00:29:59.720
I'm sure there'll be
another wave of this, but.

00:30:00.970 --> 00:30:05.130
- Well, the fact is is that you, again,

00:30:05.130 --> 00:30:10.020
whatever you can say in a
eulogy about your grandmother

00:30:10.020 --> 00:30:11.520
that doesn't come from a place

00:30:12.410 --> 00:30:13.873
rooted in Christian faith,

00:30:15.850 --> 00:30:20.740
is not going to be as
emotionally satisfying.

00:30:20.740 --> 00:30:23.450
Uncertainty is not as
emotionally satisfying

00:30:23.450 --> 00:30:25.830
as this certain hope

00:30:25.830 --> 00:30:28.677
that where you can tell everybody there,

00:30:28.677 --> 00:30:30.260
"Hey she's in a better place."

00:30:30.260 --> 00:30:31.950
Like, let's just be honest.

00:30:31.950 --> 00:30:35.370
That is the easiest thing to say, right?

00:30:35.370 --> 00:30:38.220
That is the easiest, most
comforting thing to say

00:30:38.220 --> 00:30:39.530
to a group of grieving people,

00:30:39.530 --> 00:30:42.060
is that this person is in a better place.

00:30:42.060 --> 00:30:43.490
- I do think that they're,

00:30:43.490 --> 00:30:47.480
and, you know, I'm still
thinking a lot about this.

00:30:47.480 --> 00:30:51.710
There's in terms of, you know,
my relationship with death.

00:30:51.710 --> 00:30:54.850
And I do think that
there is, I do have hope

00:30:54.850 --> 00:30:59.850
that there's more, there's
a way to embrace it,

00:31:02.209 --> 00:31:05.410
and not shy away from
it to find beauty in it,

00:31:05.410 --> 00:31:07.163
that is different.

00:31:08.610 --> 00:31:12.570
That's not something that
I'm at a place to present,

00:31:12.570 --> 00:31:16.070
but it's something that
I guess maybe ironically,

00:31:16.070 --> 00:31:17.130
I'm hopeful about.

00:31:17.130 --> 00:31:19.590
- Well, I don't think
culturally, or as a species

00:31:19.590 --> 00:31:21.630
we're there yet, honestly, right?

00:31:21.630 --> 00:31:22.730
- Culturally as-

00:31:22.730 --> 00:31:24.900
- Meaning that the cultural convention

00:31:26.026 --> 00:31:28.870
of a faith-based funeral
is still the standard

00:31:28.870 --> 00:31:31.010
even for people who
aren't really faith-based

00:31:31.010 --> 00:31:32.210
in a lot of ways, right?

00:31:35.627 --> 00:31:38.283
It's another conversation. (snickers)

00:31:39.709 --> 00:31:42.620
- I guess, to move on
to another experience.

00:31:42.620 --> 00:31:44.410
I alluded to this as well,
at the end of the year.

00:31:44.410 --> 00:31:45.950
But Christy and I walked

00:31:45.950 --> 00:31:48.430
through a really difficult time together,

00:31:48.430 --> 00:31:51.473
over many months this past year.

00:31:54.591 --> 00:31:57.610
And anxiety is not someone's fault.

00:31:57.610 --> 00:31:59.150
And it affects more than just the one

00:31:59.150 --> 00:32:00.700
who's directly experiencin' it.

00:32:02.608 --> 00:32:06.003
It was a tough stretch, pun intended.

00:32:08.256 --> 00:32:09.530
There were many sleepless nights,

00:32:09.530 --> 00:32:11.640
and there was a lot of fear.

00:32:14.750 --> 00:32:18.383
There were times when I
felt completely disoriented,

00:32:21.924 --> 00:32:23.997
and again, powerless and scared.

00:32:27.070 --> 00:32:31.223
I mean, you know, because you
and Jessie were there for us,

00:32:33.980 --> 00:32:36.453
as well as some other close friends.

00:32:40.110 --> 00:32:42.733
But throughout all of it,

00:32:45.860 --> 00:32:49.173
I didn't really ever think about praying.

00:32:50.520 --> 00:32:54.460
Now as an aside, I just wanna acknowledge

00:32:54.460 --> 00:32:59.460
that even now as I say that you know,

00:32:59.780 --> 00:33:02.070
I think it comes out like
a confession, you know.

00:33:02.070 --> 00:33:04.400
It's like, I didn't even
think about praying.

00:33:04.400 --> 00:33:06.780
And I'm not saying that I wish I did.

00:33:06.780 --> 00:33:09.670
I'm making an observation
and I wanna unpack it.

00:33:09.670 --> 00:33:12.330
But like for the second
I'm unpacking my emotions

00:33:12.330 --> 00:33:13.477
associated with even saying it,

00:33:13.477 --> 00:33:15.977
and the fact that it comes
across as a confession.

00:33:20.020 --> 00:33:20.890
I feel ashamed.

00:33:22.410 --> 00:33:23.580
I feel shame.

00:33:23.580 --> 00:33:25.453
It just wells up from inside of me.

00:33:29.090 --> 00:33:34.090
Making that statement, I
feel the feelings of failure,

00:33:35.010 --> 00:33:36.603
or being a bad person.

00:33:40.090 --> 00:33:42.210
But here's what I believe about that.

00:33:42.210 --> 00:33:46.100
I believe that that is
my inner critic talking,

00:33:46.100 --> 00:33:50.220
a version of my former self,

00:33:50.220 --> 00:33:55.220
and he is not being fair,
or kind, or correct.

00:34:01.150 --> 00:34:03.990
If I don't believe in the power of prayer,

00:34:03.990 --> 00:34:06.693
why should I feel guilty
about not praying?

00:34:11.180 --> 00:34:14.930
And so I, you know, I process that,

00:34:14.930 --> 00:34:16.410
and I say, "Come on, just come on Link,

00:34:16.410 --> 00:34:19.107
just be free, be free of this."

00:34:21.328 --> 00:34:22.730
And I mean, if it were only that easy,

00:34:22.730 --> 00:34:26.940
if it was like, incanting
some sort of a spell,

00:34:26.940 --> 00:34:30.510
or like something to release this spell,

00:34:30.510 --> 00:34:32.220
maybe is a better analogy.

00:34:32.220 --> 00:34:35.050
But I mean, you know
this, we talk about it.

00:34:35.050 --> 00:34:37.590
Sometimes we joke about it,
which I think is healthy,

00:34:37.590 --> 00:34:39.103
but I feel guilty a lot.

00:34:40.640 --> 00:34:44.253
It's not really related.

00:34:45.470 --> 00:34:48.040
I mean, in this instance,

00:34:48.040 --> 00:34:51.240
it's not related to like
specific nitpicky things.

00:34:51.240 --> 00:34:53.690
like, Oh, I'm guilty because I did that,

00:34:53.690 --> 00:34:58.550
like an OCD fixation
on individual actions.

00:34:58.550 --> 00:35:01.630
You know, it's more, I think my guilt

00:35:01.630 --> 00:35:05.690
comes from this place of
like a lingering cloud

00:35:07.080 --> 00:35:11.010
of guilt that shows up, and hangs around,

00:35:11.010 --> 00:35:13.300
and is associated with the overall idea

00:35:13.300 --> 00:35:15.180
of me leaving my faith.

00:35:15.180 --> 00:35:20.180
It's the pity of my previous
self feeling sorry for me,

00:35:23.100 --> 00:35:26.283
and also judging the now me.

00:35:29.550 --> 00:35:33.253
But I'm learning that I don't
have to listen to that voice.

00:35:34.590 --> 00:35:37.050
So I can say, you know what?

00:35:37.050 --> 00:35:40.370
Christy and I walked through

00:35:41.980 --> 00:35:45.313
an extremely challenging period of time,

00:35:49.570 --> 00:35:54.253
and you know, I didn't pray.

00:35:55.262 --> 00:35:57.048
And it wasn't this stubborn,

00:35:57.048 --> 00:35:59.940
you know, I've said what I believe,

00:35:59.940 --> 00:36:02.300
and now I got to believe
it, and I'm not gonna pray.

00:36:02.300 --> 00:36:04.850
You know, there was no
internal dialogue about that.

00:36:04.850 --> 00:36:06.045
I just-

00:36:06.045 --> 00:36:06.878
- You weren't tempted-
- I wasn't-

00:36:06.878 --> 00:36:07.850
- You weren't even tempted to.

00:36:07.850 --> 00:36:10.830
- I wasn't wrestling with reverse doubt,

00:36:10.830 --> 00:36:13.380
or like, I didn't you know,

00:36:13.380 --> 00:36:14.820
like cover my bases.

00:36:14.820 --> 00:36:17.660
Like I was at my wits end.

00:36:17.660 --> 00:36:19.820
I mean, we were having conversations,

00:36:19.820 --> 00:36:22.350
that like I would hear
what I was saying to you,

00:36:22.350 --> 00:36:25.800
and it was just, I
didn't know what I meant.

00:36:25.800 --> 00:36:27.920
You know I haven't observed,

00:36:27.920 --> 00:36:29.880
I haven't been in that situation before.

00:36:29.880 --> 00:36:31.530
I don't know that, I mean, you tell me,

00:36:31.530 --> 00:36:34.530
have you ever seen me
or Christy at a place

00:36:34.530 --> 00:36:36.573
where it was like, I don't know,

00:36:37.656 --> 00:36:40.550
and it seems like a different
person like at kind of a loss.

00:36:40.550 --> 00:36:43.400
- You were incapacitated.

00:36:43.400 --> 00:36:44.233
- Right.

00:36:44.233 --> 00:36:45.080
- Yeah.

00:36:45.080 --> 00:36:48.670
- And, you know, I think that is a moment

00:36:48.670 --> 00:36:51.790
where, you know it cinematically speaking

00:36:51.790 --> 00:36:55.443
where the character would
drop to their knees and say,

00:36:57.627 --> 00:37:00.583
"Oh God, I'm sorry that I forsook you."

00:37:04.980 --> 00:37:07.940
You know like a moment of
repentance or something,

00:37:07.940 --> 00:37:12.120
or just a moment of
desperate prayer, you know.

00:37:12.120 --> 00:37:16.853
Like if, you have the
cinematic bargaining with God.

00:37:17.710 --> 00:37:20.753
- Well, and I think that's
because that's the narrative

00:37:20.753 --> 00:37:23.000
that we believe, and I think-

00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:25.890
- Yeah, it'll cut, you'll hit rock bottom.

00:37:25.890 --> 00:37:27.750
- And I think it's what a lot
of people have said about us.

00:37:27.750 --> 00:37:29.270
It's just like, okay, well those boys

00:37:29.270 --> 00:37:30.723
are riding high right now,

00:37:31.576 --> 00:37:33.030
but you know the moment
that the bottom drops out

00:37:33.030 --> 00:37:34.930
from one of them, some tragedy happens,

00:37:34.930 --> 00:37:37.920
is like that's the moment
that they'll turn around

00:37:37.920 --> 00:37:39.680
and come back to God.

00:37:39.680 --> 00:37:41.343
And I-
- And I just don't-

00:37:41.343 --> 00:37:43.320
- I don't wanna skip over
the inner voice thing,

00:37:43.320 --> 00:37:46.724
because I if you're not
gonna come back to it,

00:37:46.724 --> 00:37:49.010
because I think that's really significant

00:37:49.010 --> 00:37:51.483
for so many people, the former voice.

00:37:52.430 --> 00:37:54.480
And especially as somebody who struggles,

00:37:54.480 --> 00:37:57.440
with, I don't necessarily, I
struggle with a lot of shame.

00:37:57.440 --> 00:38:00.313
I'm the king of shame, but
guilt is not so much my thing.

00:38:01.380 --> 00:38:05.110
But for somebody who struggles with guilt,

00:38:05.110 --> 00:38:07.170
being a part of a religious system,

00:38:07.170 --> 00:38:10.960
especially in our experience,
evangelical Christianity,

00:38:10.960 --> 00:38:13.053
it's like steroids for the guilty, right.

00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:15.960
It's high octane.

00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:19.370
And of course, I understand that like,

00:38:19.370 --> 00:38:20.810
I remember being an evangelical,

00:38:20.810 --> 00:38:22.930
and saying that like, "Listen,
no, we're all about grace.

00:38:22.930 --> 00:38:26.010
It's the Catholics, or the Jews.

00:38:26.010 --> 00:38:27.670
They're the ones who are all about works.

00:38:27.670 --> 00:38:29.130
And they're the ones who are guilt-ridden,

00:38:29.130 --> 00:38:30.520
but we live in the freedom

00:38:30.520 --> 00:38:34.460
that comes with a grace-based
relationship with Christ."

00:38:34.460 --> 00:38:36.810
And it's like a fun thing to say,

00:38:36.810 --> 00:38:39.160
but in reality, there's
still so much pressure,

00:38:39.160 --> 00:38:40.760
and there's still so much expectation.

00:38:40.760 --> 00:38:43.240
My wife is an expert
at talking about this,

00:38:43.240 --> 00:38:45.810
about what it's like
to be somebody with OCD

00:38:45.810 --> 00:38:47.763
in the midst of a religious system.

00:38:48.800 --> 00:38:51.010
But one of the things that,

00:38:51.010 --> 00:38:52.630
so I also do the same thing.

00:38:52.630 --> 00:38:57.630
I have that former self
who's constantly judging me.

00:38:57.650 --> 00:38:58.880
I think it was one of the reasons

00:38:58.880 --> 00:39:01.890
that I can talk about
these things in a way,

00:39:01.890 --> 00:39:04.040
that connects with people
who are still in the church,

00:39:04.040 --> 00:39:06.560
because I have a really,
really strong connection

00:39:06.560 --> 00:39:08.320
with my former self.

00:39:08.320 --> 00:39:10.000
But the change in relationship,

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:13.050
and this is something that
has come through therapy.

00:39:13.050 --> 00:39:14.340
My therapist has helped me see this,

00:39:14.340 --> 00:39:16.760
is that what you're talking about

00:39:16.760 --> 00:39:18.180
is looking at that former self,

00:39:18.180 --> 00:39:19.630
and saying that former self is wrong.

00:39:19.630 --> 00:39:22.790
That former self is being judgmental.

00:39:22.790 --> 00:39:25.273
That former self is not being kind.

00:39:25.273 --> 00:39:26.930
And I don't have to listen
to that former self.

00:39:26.930 --> 00:39:30.640
I think one additional step

00:39:30.640 --> 00:39:32.430
that has been really helpful for me

00:39:33.733 --> 00:39:35.810
is having sympathy.

00:39:35.810 --> 00:39:37.110
- Yes, well I would say-

00:39:37.110 --> 00:39:39.170
- Or having empathy-
- I would say empathy.

00:39:39.170 --> 00:39:40.850
- Having empathy for that former self.

00:39:40.850 --> 00:39:44.362
- Well, yeah and absolutely.

00:39:44.362 --> 00:39:46.423
And so I'm glad you, you teed that up,

00:39:47.323 --> 00:39:50.160
because that is something
that I'm working on.

00:39:50.160 --> 00:39:54.170
It's like, okay, I know
that this inner critic,

00:39:54.170 --> 00:39:59.100
this inner voice, this
former self, is harsh.

00:39:59.100 --> 00:40:01.860
But I don't have to respond that way,

00:40:01.860 --> 00:40:03.770
because I can also see

00:40:03.770 --> 00:40:08.770
that there's, his motive is to protect me.

00:40:10.860 --> 00:40:14.790
It's a part of myself, yes from my past,

00:40:14.790 --> 00:40:16.910
but it's still a part of who I am,

00:40:16.910 --> 00:40:19.600
that's trying to protect
me from something.

00:40:19.600 --> 00:40:21.100
But it's like, okay, you know what?

00:40:21.100 --> 00:40:25.190
I appreciate what you're
trying to do here.

00:40:25.190 --> 00:40:29.360
And I know you're just trying
to help me and protect me.

00:40:29.360 --> 00:40:31.100
And, you know, there
is work for me to say,

00:40:31.100 --> 00:40:32.910
okay protect me from what,

00:40:32.910 --> 00:40:34.310
and let's get into those specifics.

00:40:34.310 --> 00:40:36.810
But to have an empathetic response,

00:40:36.810 --> 00:40:38.960
that's like, what you know what?

00:40:38.960 --> 00:40:43.230
Thank you, but I don't have
to take action on this,

00:40:43.230 --> 00:40:45.653
and you are not all of me.

00:40:47.700 --> 00:40:52.297
So yeah, that is something
that in therapy, I'm seeing.

00:40:55.240 --> 00:40:56.570
And I might hit on it a little bit,

00:40:56.570 --> 00:40:59.744
more with this third experience.

00:40:59.744 --> 00:41:00.960
But yeah, you're exactly right,

00:41:00.960 --> 00:41:02.610
and I'm glad you brought that up.

00:41:04.225 --> 00:41:06.463
So just to get back to the trial,

00:41:07.310 --> 00:41:08.470
or however you wanna put it,

00:41:08.470 --> 00:41:10.577
like what Christy and I went through.

00:41:10.577 --> 00:41:12.873
And I mean, I don't wanna,

00:41:14.350 --> 00:41:17.080
I'm not gonna share all the
details of it at this point.

00:41:17.080 --> 00:41:19.430
I think, you know, a lot of
that's her story to tell,

00:41:19.430 --> 00:41:22.790
and it's, or maybe our story
to tell together at some point.

00:41:22.790 --> 00:41:24.960
Who knows, but for now,
you know I'll just say

00:41:24.960 --> 00:41:28.850
that it was, Christy who was dealing

00:41:28.850 --> 00:41:32.543
with a debilitating level of anxiety,

00:41:34.170 --> 00:41:38.450
you know with all the
circumstances that are happening.

00:41:38.450 --> 00:41:40.440
Like a certain level of health anxiety

00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:45.440
that then just became, yeah,
it just became debilitating.

00:41:45.650 --> 00:41:47.060
And there were panic attacks,

00:41:47.060 --> 00:41:52.060
and there was, you know, it's
not as simple as Googling

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:53.650
how to deal with a panic attack,

00:41:53.650 --> 00:41:56.370
or how to deal with health anxiety.

00:41:56.370 --> 00:41:59.060
You know, it's like you
find yourself in a place

00:41:59.060 --> 00:42:00.343
where it's okay.

00:42:01.593 --> 00:42:03.630
The natural tendency is
a downward spiral here,

00:42:03.630 --> 00:42:06.770
that then we've gotta start,

00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:08.060
find the right people to talk to,

00:42:08.060 --> 00:42:13.060
and the right things to do,
to back back out of this,

00:42:14.970 --> 00:42:17.523
or really, I would say to walk through it,

00:42:17.523 --> 00:42:20.063
to a healthier place.

00:42:23.203 --> 00:42:27.370
But as far as it relates
to my spiritual journey,

00:42:27.370 --> 00:42:29.983
just kind of processing
how I did respond to it.

00:42:31.670 --> 00:42:36.543
Yeah, I didn't pray to, or curse God.

00:42:37.880 --> 00:42:42.610
I just, I mean, I just
responded practically.

00:42:42.610 --> 00:42:44.640
You know, I did everything that I could.

00:42:44.640 --> 00:42:48.320
I just, I mean when I look back on it,

00:42:48.320 --> 00:42:52.963
I would say that I met
the situation with love.

00:42:54.900 --> 00:42:58.093
I felt as if I was acting
on instinct at the time.

00:42:59.290 --> 00:43:02.140
But I realize now that it was,
I mean it was simply love.

00:43:03.030 --> 00:43:06.533
I love Christy with
everything that I've got.

00:43:07.840 --> 00:43:11.563
And it was then that I,

00:43:12.490 --> 00:43:15.363
I mean I really knew it
at those points, you know.

00:43:16.400 --> 00:43:20.050
And we leaned on friends
and professionals,

00:43:20.050 --> 00:43:25.050
to help us, and they did,
and we got through it.

00:43:27.090 --> 00:43:31.020
And I mean, it's not,
they're residual effects

00:43:31.020 --> 00:43:32.830
and there's some long-term things

00:43:33.849 --> 00:43:34.997
that we deal with associated with it,

00:43:34.997 --> 00:43:36.890
and that we're more ready for now.

00:43:36.890 --> 00:43:39.920
But when the worst of it was behind us,

00:43:39.920 --> 00:43:42.463
I was extremely grateful.

00:43:45.020 --> 00:43:47.393
But I didn't thank God per se.

00:43:50.098 --> 00:43:51.148
I didn't take credit.

00:43:55.850 --> 00:43:58.550
And I'll quiet that voice that tells me,

00:43:58.550 --> 00:44:00.610
that I should feel guilty

00:44:00.610 --> 00:44:04.893
for not giving God the glory, so to speak.

00:44:06.440 --> 00:44:11.290
I mean, maybe somebody would
listen to our description

00:44:11.290 --> 00:44:15.050
to that inner voice and
say that that's God,

00:44:15.050 --> 00:44:17.140
or that's the Holy Spirit.

00:44:17.140 --> 00:44:21.662
And, you know, but I don't
know, but I do not think so.

00:44:21.662 --> 00:44:24.979
You know, because of the outcome

00:44:24.979 --> 00:44:28.961
of what that voice is telling
me, the application of it,

00:44:28.961 --> 00:44:31.670
it's just not, that's not it.

00:44:31.670 --> 00:44:34.650
- Well, and as someone

00:44:34.650 --> 00:44:36.560
who is also married to someone

00:44:36.560 --> 00:44:39.860
who has had a lifelong
struggle with anxiety,

00:44:39.860 --> 00:44:41.340
in a struggle with anxiety

00:44:41.340 --> 00:44:46.340
that has been debilitating at times,

00:44:47.190 --> 00:44:49.930
and has happened inside the church,

00:44:49.930 --> 00:44:52.700
and, you know, with great faith,

00:44:52.700 --> 00:44:55.943
and then outside of the church
with no faith in that system.

00:45:00.633 --> 00:45:02.353
There is, in my experience,

00:45:03.470 --> 00:45:05.703
there is a tendency to,

00:45:06.840 --> 00:45:10.060
because you have the ability to pray.

00:45:10.060 --> 00:45:12.700
And because you do have the ability to,

00:45:12.700 --> 00:45:13.730
when you're at your wits end,

00:45:13.730 --> 00:45:18.283
to sort of give it over to the
Lord, to invite God into it,

00:45:20.310 --> 00:45:25.310
sometimes that leads to
excluding or bypassing

00:45:26.660 --> 00:45:30.090
the practical steps that
would actually be helpful.

00:45:30.090 --> 00:45:32.120
- Yeah, we had to drill in very deeply

00:45:32.120 --> 00:45:36.880
and specifically with
professionals involved,

00:45:36.880 --> 00:45:39.090
with therapist and psychiatrist

00:45:39.090 --> 00:45:40.010
and things that, you know,

00:45:40.010 --> 00:45:43.530
there's no embarrassment
associated with saying that.

00:45:43.530 --> 00:45:46.490
And in the same way that if
you had a physical condition,

00:45:46.490 --> 00:45:51.110
if you had, you know, that
you would drill in medically,

00:45:51.110 --> 00:45:52.270
and you would do everything you could,

00:45:52.270 --> 00:45:53.730
and you can just resort.
- But there are people.

00:45:53.730 --> 00:45:55.500
There are people within the church-

00:45:55.500 --> 00:45:57.050
- To only a spiritual exercise.

00:45:58.074 --> 00:45:58.907
- Like prayer.
- There are people

00:45:58.907 --> 00:45:59.740
within the church.
- Like prayer.

00:45:59.740 --> 00:46:02.231
- And we weren't, we don't
come from a tradition

00:46:02.231 --> 00:46:04.720
that is like anti-science and anti,

00:46:04.720 --> 00:46:05.790
I mean little anti-science,

00:46:05.790 --> 00:46:07.730
but not like anti-doctor necessarily.

00:46:07.730 --> 00:46:09.600
I mean, it's kind of
becoming more anti-doctor,

00:46:09.600 --> 00:46:10.520
with COVID and everything.

00:46:10.520 --> 00:46:15.520
But there is this, there
is a little bit of a,

00:46:16.660 --> 00:46:20.870
hmm, oh you didn't, God
didn't do this for you.

00:46:20.870 --> 00:46:24.440
You kinda had to go to the world
to get your problem solved.

00:46:24.440 --> 00:46:25.350
And there's some people,

00:46:25.350 --> 00:46:26.730
depending on what tradition they're in,

00:46:26.730 --> 00:46:31.640
that are that live in
debilitating mental illness,

00:46:31.640 --> 00:46:34.669
because they cannot-
- Specifically-

00:46:34.669 --> 00:46:35.502
- Get out of the system.

00:46:35.502 --> 00:46:37.343
- Especially mental illness,

00:46:40.792 --> 00:46:42.420
because those type of things

00:46:42.420 --> 00:46:47.420
are the unseen problems and challenges,

00:46:47.700 --> 00:46:50.590
are the ones that can
be easily written off

00:46:50.590 --> 00:46:55.590
with a prayer or a proverb,
or you know, some teaching.

00:46:55.960 --> 00:47:00.960
And I, you know, having
benefited from therapist,

00:47:02.550 --> 00:47:06.827
and psychiatrist, and
psychological treatment,

00:47:09.705 --> 00:47:12.563
it's just not the, you know,

00:47:14.780 --> 00:47:19.240
it doesn't pinpoint the
specific problems, you know.

00:47:19.240 --> 00:47:21.750
I think that it requires
a professional to do that.

00:47:21.750 --> 00:47:24.966
It's not just something

00:47:24.966 --> 00:47:27.080
that you can apply just
to general platitudes.

00:47:27.080 --> 00:47:28.070
- And I'll admit something,

00:47:28.070 --> 00:47:30.920
that this probably get me in
trouble, but I'm used to it.

00:47:32.320 --> 00:47:36.950
Now, when we seek treatment
from professionals,

00:47:36.950 --> 00:47:39.490
whether they be therapist,
psychologist, psychiatrist,

00:47:39.490 --> 00:47:40.940
either for ourselves, or for other people

00:47:40.940 --> 00:47:42.703
that we know who are going through things.

00:47:44.170 --> 00:47:47.610
I actually, at this point in my life,

00:47:47.610 --> 00:47:49.470
I try to steer away from people

00:47:49.470 --> 00:47:51.140
who have a faith-based approach,

00:47:51.140 --> 00:47:56.020
or who really bring a Christian worldview

00:47:56.020 --> 00:48:00.840
into their treatment again,
because my experience

00:48:00.840 --> 00:48:03.840
is that it's like filling in the gap

00:48:03.840 --> 00:48:06.743
with something that isn't
actually going to be helpful.

00:48:09.560 --> 00:48:11.880
It's like, let's set that aside.

00:48:11.880 --> 00:48:13.390
Let's set that uncertain,

00:48:13.390 --> 00:48:16.700
I don't know if praying does anything,

00:48:16.700 --> 00:48:19.120
giving it to God may do nothing.

00:48:19.120 --> 00:48:23.630
Let's take the practical,
tested approach to this problem

00:48:24.640 --> 00:48:26.950
so we can actually solve it.

00:48:26.950 --> 00:48:28.210
And again, I'm not saying

00:48:28.210 --> 00:48:30.070
that having a Christian
worldview is a bad thing.

00:48:30.070 --> 00:48:31.420
I'm just saying when somebody is,

00:48:31.420 --> 00:48:36.020
if I've got a cancer
doctor, who's working on me,

00:48:36.020 --> 00:48:38.787
I don't want that doctor to say,

00:48:38.787 --> 00:48:39.620
"You know what?

00:48:39.620 --> 00:48:41.660
I'm doing this operation on you,

00:48:41.660 --> 00:48:44.760
but I'm really praying that it goes well."

00:48:44.760 --> 00:48:48.813
Or do I just want him to say,
"I'm going to do it well,

00:48:49.690 --> 00:48:52.280
and it's all on me to do it well."

00:48:52.280 --> 00:48:53.113
Again, I mean-

00:48:53.113 --> 00:48:54.784
- I well I don't, yeah.

00:48:54.784 --> 00:48:55.617
I'm sure that there's pastors who,

00:48:55.617 --> 00:48:57.910
if people come to them
from their congregation

00:48:57.910 --> 00:48:59.577
with problems, they'll say,

00:48:59.577 --> 00:49:03.870
"With this particular challenge
that you're sharing with me,

00:49:03.870 --> 00:49:07.000
you need to see a
psychiatrist, a psychologist,

00:49:07.000 --> 00:49:09.090
a therapist, you know."

00:49:09.090 --> 00:49:12.630
But that wasn't our experience
when we were growing up.

00:49:12.630 --> 00:49:13.620
And you wouldn't even,

00:49:13.620 --> 00:49:15.560
even if you had to go
to one of those places,

00:49:15.560 --> 00:49:18.040
you would just use, you would
say, I went to counseling.

00:49:18.040 --> 00:49:21.161
You would use a code word,
and it would be stigmatized.

00:49:21.161 --> 00:49:21.994
And it would be-
- There's like a lotta

00:49:21.994 --> 00:49:24.149
prayer-based counseling,
and that kind of thing.

00:49:24.149 --> 00:49:25.900
That's acceptable.

00:49:25.900 --> 00:49:28.940
You can do that, but if
it's just the practical,

00:49:28.940 --> 00:49:31.930
scientific stuff, then
I don't know about that.

00:49:31.930 --> 00:49:34.563
That's kind of the attitude that we had.

00:49:35.750 --> 00:49:39.750
- So, I'll move to the
third and final experience

00:49:39.750 --> 00:49:41.970
that I wanted to share today.

00:49:41.970 --> 00:49:42.860
And that's...

00:49:46.810 --> 00:49:49.962
and there's, yeah the details of this

00:49:49.962 --> 00:49:52.660
are not my story to tell.

00:49:52.660 --> 00:49:54.713
So, you know, forgive me for,

00:49:56.480 --> 00:49:58.890
or don't forgive me, just
I know you understand

00:49:58.890 --> 00:50:00.507
that the way that I'm telling this,

00:50:00.507 --> 00:50:02.857
and the details I'm
putting in and leaving out.

00:50:04.160 --> 00:50:07.440
My mom is currently facing

00:50:07.440 --> 00:50:12.440
what may be the most difficult
trial of her entire life.

00:50:13.540 --> 00:50:18.217
Every day, all year long, for years now.

00:50:20.220 --> 00:50:25.202
And again, we have the COVID of at all.

00:50:25.202 --> 00:50:27.890
I'm her only child.

00:50:27.890 --> 00:50:30.463
I don't know if you could
tell I was an only child.

00:50:30.463 --> 00:50:32.460
- (snickers) Choke on it.

00:50:32.460 --> 00:50:33.593
- And (chuckles) yeah,

00:50:34.730 --> 00:50:37.973
and I've not been able to be with her.

00:50:40.570 --> 00:50:44.773
And I try my best to get
better at talking on the phone,

00:50:46.176 --> 00:50:48.112
and to understand her situation,

00:50:48.112 --> 00:50:50.763
and assess what needs to
be done, and to help her.

00:50:52.420 --> 00:50:57.420
But I'm stuck on the opposite
coast because of the pandemic.

00:50:57.442 --> 00:50:59.342
And so I, you know, I worry about her.

00:51:00.730 --> 00:51:04.033
Again, it's that feeling of helplessness,

00:51:05.845 --> 00:51:08.720
and, you know, I feel bad for going weeks,

00:51:08.720 --> 00:51:10.293
in between talking to her.

00:51:14.220 --> 00:51:16.393
But when I do talk to her,

00:51:17.700 --> 00:51:20.603
she's always happy to hear my voice,

00:51:21.460 --> 00:51:25.780
and she doesn't wanna
dump her problems on me,

00:51:25.780 --> 00:51:28.640
but what else is there to talk about,

00:51:28.640 --> 00:51:31.200
because this has become
her entire life, you know?

00:51:31.200 --> 00:51:34.140
So we talk about how she's doing,

00:51:34.140 --> 00:51:39.140
and I try to really hear
her and offer encouragement,

00:51:39.660 --> 00:51:43.263
and help think through things.

00:51:45.660 --> 00:51:50.660
And it's become, you
know like I just realized

00:51:51.930 --> 00:51:54.460
how difficult, and the toll

00:51:54.460 --> 00:51:56.513
this was also taking on me, you know.

00:52:00.742 --> 00:52:02.940
And we were on the phone recently,

00:52:02.940 --> 00:52:06.410
and she relayed a conversation

00:52:06.410 --> 00:52:08.983
that she had had with someone else.

00:52:10.132 --> 00:52:12.380
And I'm not gonna tell you the story,

00:52:12.380 --> 00:52:16.253
because this story was meant for me.

00:52:17.490 --> 00:52:18.323
And you know what?

00:52:18.323 --> 00:52:21.960
When she told me the
conversations she had,

00:52:21.960 --> 00:52:23.283
she didn't build it up,

00:52:24.604 --> 00:52:27.254
or maybe she didn't even
realize the poignancy of it.

00:52:28.610 --> 00:52:31.960
But again, I'm not sharing,

00:52:31.960 --> 00:52:34.540
I don't wanna share her situation.

00:52:34.540 --> 00:52:39.540
But what she shared was,
it was heartbreaking,

00:52:39.660 --> 00:52:44.310
and it was honest, and it was beautiful,

00:52:44.310 --> 00:52:47.943
and it was tragic, and it was inspiring,

00:52:49.140 --> 00:52:51.493
and it stopped me dead in my tracks.

00:52:53.790 --> 00:52:57.923
And in this moment I realized,

00:52:59.980 --> 00:53:02.803
not only was I being there for my mom,

00:53:03.662 --> 00:53:06.380
but even with all that
she was going through,

00:53:06.380 --> 00:53:09.423
she was also still being there for me.

00:53:12.611 --> 00:53:17.103
And the specifics of her story,

00:53:20.840 --> 00:53:25.670
and what she went through,
and was telling me about,

00:53:25.670 --> 00:53:30.293
it painted this perfect picture of love.

00:53:33.782 --> 00:53:36.177
And she showed me a type
of love to aspire to.

00:53:38.610 --> 00:53:41.780
And I you know, I've thought
a lot about it since then,

00:53:41.780 --> 00:53:44.530
and I've realized

00:53:46.570 --> 00:53:49.713
that this is my spiritual practice.

00:53:54.120 --> 00:53:55.753
Love will be my guide.

00:54:00.692 --> 00:54:04.340
You know, I'm gonna make up
my mind to be introspective,

00:54:04.340 --> 00:54:08.823
to not miss moments like
that, as much as I can.

00:54:09.893 --> 00:54:14.197
And I will not tear myself
apart from the inside.

00:54:16.660 --> 00:54:21.617
I will love myself, and I will
love others as much as I can.

00:54:22.938 --> 00:54:24.680
And I will live the life that I have.

00:54:24.680 --> 00:54:25.513
And...

00:54:31.220 --> 00:54:33.063
that's my spiritual practice.

00:54:34.850 --> 00:54:39.850
At a point when, and so I don't know.

00:54:39.920 --> 00:54:41.810
I don't know how people will process that,

00:54:41.810 --> 00:54:46.810
as glib, or elegant or, you
know (chuckles) whatever.

00:54:47.350 --> 00:54:51.190
But for me, you know, when
you boil something down

00:54:51.190 --> 00:54:54.250
